  "release_url": "https://github.com/SadPull/LLM-benders-SUC/releases/tag/v0.36.0",
  "changes": [
    "Escalation tier: when a regular (HTTP) LLM call improves UB by less than llm_escalation_gain or fails, one isolated Codex CLI request (fresh session, temporary CODEX_HOME, --ephemeral) runs in parallel; two failures disable only this tier",
    "LLM feedback lists ramp-reachable capacity shortfall hours for dispatch-infeasible candidates; the system prompt explains the bound",
    "result.json keeps each call's request base (base_u), format counts and per-candidate outcomes, raw changes and rebase results",
    "Removed: resume path (RESUME_FROM, run_suc(resume_state=), restore()), manual file-exchange channel (agent_bridge.py), archived qubo()/quantize() with theta_step/penalty/reserve_scale, dormant audit hooks, unused optimize() parameters",
    "Result keys removed: summary scope/audit_status/resume_source/segment_*/new_llm_calls/block_sa_calls (segment_wall_seconds renamed solver_wall_seconds); manifest cold_start/inherited_evidence/resume_source; progress resume_cursor/segment_elapsed_seconds; in-progress status reads RUNNING",
    "LLM prompt drops constant fields optimality_cuts, hamming_to_incumbent, infeasible_diagnostics and advice_routing",
    "Proof process fingerprints the model once per perspective round (IEEE118 first round 0.83 s -> 0.01 s)",
    "Block-SA diagnostics keep scalars and hashes only (classic10, 8 SA calls: 0.65 MB -> 0.09 MB); search_statistics unchanged",
    "solve() split into named phases; BlockSearch/WholeDay, LLM parsing, advisor tiers, entry point and option checks reorganised"
  ],
