  "findings": {
    "incremental_output_fix": "IEEE118 SA+DeepSeek improved from +4.934% (v0.35.0 full-matrix output) to +2.046%..+2.691% across four runs with incremental output and per-candidate validation",
    "shortfall_feedback": "With ramp-reachable shortfall feedback, dispatch-feasible candidates rose from 6/12 to 15/16, but the final UB (+2.354%) was not better in this single run",
    "escalation_pair": "DeepSeek+astra reached +1.465% vs +2.691% for DeepSeek alone, but 91.1% of the hybrid decrease came from the first DeepSeek call before escalation; astra contributed 0.5%",
    "stall_probe": "On the same stalled-state prompt: gpt-6-astra 4/4 feasible, best +1.490%; deepseek-v4.1-flash 2/4, best +1.901% (one call each)",
    "sa_baseline": "Plain SA gave the identical UB 3948959.48 (+7.515%) on ffaaf1d and three earlier commits"
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Single seed and a single run per group; DeepSeek reasoning is stochastic (DeepSeek-alone runs span +2.046%..+2.691%)",
    "The hybrid-vs-alone difference is dominated by the first regular call and cannot be attributed to the escalation tier",
    "All runs in this release used the pre-cleanup prompt; results after the prompt cleanup are not byte-comparable",
    "Reference optimum (3672938.50) is used only for after-the-fact comparison"
  ],
